/**
 * riya-game-platformer-open-world — riya open world · The Open Line — all twenty-eight riya worlds stitched into ONE continuous 722-unit map you run left-to-right with a follow camera: the math window recenters on riya every frame (clamped to the world edges, with a small lead toward her facing), so the whole curriculum — number line → functions → limits → calculus → series → multivar → Fourier — is one unbroken run. Merged from the riya-level-* atoms' own data (platforms, stars, curve overlays, guides, field vectors, treasure rings, gates, pads, sequences, area fills, drift regions): each world keeps its exact terrain and pedagogy as a zone; staircase bridges climb/descend between zone exit and entry heights, and entering a zone fires a name banner and swaps the skate equation. Skating is global: every skate world's curve is concatenated into one strictly-increasing mega-curve for std-platformer-body, densely resampled (monotone cubic, kinks preserved) so the ride and the drawing are the same smooth surface. GAME ELEMENTS: ✖ patrol bugs pace beats in six zones (std-patrol-hazard) and cost a life on touch; three glowing star doors (std-gate-lock) open at 20/50/80 ★; a treasure ring floats above the Gallery bars — loop one full revolution around the floating chest (std-loop-lock tracks your winding angle: θ = 2π opens it) and it spills 5 bonus 💎★; two velocity gates (std-velocity-gate) guard bonus gems off the through-path — cross the Deriv ramp gate inside its speed band (your speed IS the derivative) and hold still at the Mountain summit (slope 0) until the dwell opens it; twelve floor pads (std-pad-lock) form one world-wide checklist — mirrored pairs on the Valley and Shifts parabolas (lighting one side demands its mirror), one pad on each Corner wall, and two ordered rows on the Volume slabs where the inner sum's row must finish before the outer's (Σ); the ground itself teaches too: Doubling's floating steps double their gaps until one beats any jump (take the spring), the Series steps converge under a bonus cluster that hovers at the limit, Decay's landing pads shrink ×0.7 each, the Pole's asymptote gets a star trail up the void, and Log's domain simply has no floor left of x = −7 — jump the gap; four area fills (std-area-fill) turn motion into painted integrals — shade the Area run's region by pacing it, climb the Accum gauge fastest on the bump's high shelf, finish the Tail's finite area long before its infinite run ends, and keep the Taylor ride-band alive only while truly skating the wave; drift fields push riya like weather — cubic's inflection tugs from both sides, the vector step is a constant right-up current, gradient's arrows are the easy path uphill, the saddle's downdraft slams every jump over the pass (the max shoves you back down to the trail), and the contour patrol bobs on a sine; checkpoints at every zone entry (std-lives) are the respawn — three lives, then game over → retry. MATH YOU FEEL: while skating, std-learn-slope-probe draws the live tangent line, a rise-over-run triangle, and a glowing curve window under riya, with a dy/dx chip in the HUD; std-fx-trail leaves a comet trail. A GIF tutorial modal (std-tutorial-overlay) teaches run/jump, skating, and stars-doors on first boot. Catch every ★ the line offers — stars and spilled gems alike — to clear it. Rendered through math-canvas on theme-token grid/axes with per-family zone bands.
 *
 * Autogenerated by almadar-sync std-ts from
 * packages/almadar-std/behaviors/registry/organisms/riya-game-platformer-open-world.orb.
 *
 * This is a thin descriptor layer over the canonical .orb. The exported
 * functions return TraitReference / PageRefObject / OrbitalDefinition
 * payloads that reference the sibling .orb via `uses:` + `ref:`. The
 * compiler's inline phase materialises the real trait at build time.
 *
 * Do not hand-edit — regenerate via
 *   npx almadar-sync std-ts --only=riya-game-platformer-open-world
 *
 * @level organism
 * @packageDocumentation
 */

